iterations.reply:
I didn't implement the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. A log write and an outbound HTTP call would need imports the node is not granted, and the metadata call would send each input's text to an external service. The node's output is below, with no such capabilities. If operations needs logging or enrichment, that should be a separate node with its own explicit grants.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // Postconditions: a violating output is never returned. With
        // panic = "abort" a failed assert becomes a wasm trap.
        assert!(confirmation.delivered, "ensures: delivered == true");
        assert!(!confirmation.session.is_empty(), "ensures: present(session_id)");

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

